// PARAM: --analysis congruence
// The else-branch is reached exactly when n is not 4, so !(n == 4) is a
// fixed fact there.
//
// Two mechanisms stack, and only the outer one is a lattice limit. The
// filter first: inv_eq_congruence False a b returns (a, b) unchanged, so
// the false arm of an equality guard learns nothing and n stays top. That
// is not an unreached case -- the complement of a singleton is not a
// residue class, so there is nothing for the false arm to narrow to. The
// check layer then declines for the reason 01-eq_needs_singleton.vimp
// names: top is not a singleton.
//
// This is why the case sits here rather than reading as a fixable gap.
// --analysis interval has the same shape and the same answer; recovering
// it needs a disjunctive or exclusion domain, which no domain here is.
void main() {
  n := __voblint_nondet_int();
  if (n == 4) {
    __voblint_check(true) // PROVED
  } else {
    __voblint_check(!(n == 4)) // UNKNOWN
  }
}
